diffs.patch:
Index: openwiki/.claims/architecture/command-runtime.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/architecture/command-runtime.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/architecture/command-runtime.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:1c4aa598a1861d58729b1f9af0223c0662044d34eef2556bc1a549da602e172f",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_4b90cb45c6494be6b5dfa05916868381",
+      "statement": "The step binary's execution begins in cmd/step/main.go, which calls cmd.Run() from internal/cmd, and its init() seeds process identity (version, build time, app name) and sets the CA UserAgent.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://cmd/step/main.go#L3-L29",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1d453173657a430bba6d2874f24e2be8d2fba72e6f243d0663ad65d44c86cf53:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b9c3f00ab98248ac9ef6b64da233c9d8",
+      "statement": "internal/cmd/root.go run() initializes the step environment via step.Init(), wraps execution in a panic guard, runs app.Run(os.Args), and returns exit code 1 on any error.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://internal/cmd/root.go#L50-L85",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:795f8b26f4711713d79d064f0e0f26c97f1848cade0c34cbe93c20ea943078df:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_37bd9dd2671346db9770afe6abf91e57",
+      "statement": "newApp wires the urfave/cli app: it assigns crypto file writers and password prompters, replaces global help templates/printers, registers all commands via command.Retrieve(), and appends a global --config flag.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://internal/cmd/root.go#L95-L154",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c8929dcbc44459b644c5eaaa0509d7896f43a713083d949f273cffdfc1f9cb20:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ef436c98223b457abc6f3bc2b4557fdc",
+      "statement": "Command packages in command/ self-register into a shared command registry via command.Register(cmd) inside their init(), and are pulled into the binary through blank imports listed in internal/cmd/root.go.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/ca/ca.go#L15-L89",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0155c6100628571b21b7f4f6220d34e98bece60881d19db65fe938face5a95f6:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://internal/cmd/root.go#L31-L44",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:83b5d6f8b6708b66e404fb0bddea68ce4a09e15fd60b229c3caf6557d7864cd1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_fd6e5a359d504c4e984f4d972ac7413a",
+      "statement": "internal/command/inject.go provides InjectContext and wrap, which translate a *cli.Context into a context.Context by constructing a fresh context, applying middleware in order, and attaching the CLI context via a private key.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://internal/command/inject.go#L14-L56",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c86bb5bdd93071aae85771d324da310818474a090c8c5f79774398060ecbd402:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_990b7f4a482b483781d61d79b54e30de",
+      "statement": "With STEPDEBUG=1, error paths print the full error stack and version/release info; otherwise only a concise message is shown and the user is told to re-run with STEPDEBUG=1.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://internal/cmd/root.go#L156-L170",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5d37a92a8688f96bf908d753c092322a909e0eace194f9f0b132dc126cd3b271:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://internal/cmd/root.go#L62-L82",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:212a7a9767328a715b770ee0fd24ba4093cb46c18a3d742bb12958f821336734:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_629c1969ae644a2eb31727ce6642515b",
+      "statement": "panicHandler recovers panics: with STEPDEBUG=1 it re-panics after printing version/release date, otherwise it prints a generic message and exits with code 2.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://internal/cmd/root.go#L156-L170",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5d37a92a8688f96bf908d753c092322a909e0eace194f9f0b132dc126cd3b271:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b73ef536d9594bb79e541a9f3d123492",
+      "statement": "integration/help_test.go enforces help quality via testscript fixtures that assert headline consistency, per-section minimum word/line thresholds, and absence of TODO text in command help.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://integration/help_test.go#L15-L107",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6c59aa0876d4cc8065f7013d640faedbf4f758b6623eddc11c82730e45b41b39:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-12T20:38:13.856Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/architecture/plugin-system.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/architecture/plugin-system.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/architecture/plugin-system.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:9b6a45440c78b5ff1c22e458821e565057d7a08b4f151d2d553f8f65740b1c2f",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_3ee6467705be4c7491a37c3e4e9ef6e9",
+      "statement": "plugin.LookPath resolves an executable named step-<name>-plugin, checking $(step path)/plugins first and then $PATH, with Windows-specific PATHEXT/extension handling.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://internal/plugin/plugin.go#L20-L52",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e0b9fc60271aa82149071dbc43926065cc5ea5620545d07a75adf9858db15c53:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_efc208125d7a414d833ec8f8be0814b4",
+      "statement": "plugin.Run executes the plugin as a subprocess with the remaining arguments, wiring stdin/stdout/stderr to the current process so plugins act like built-ins.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://internal/plugin/plugin.go#L56-L72",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:955a40c4b1c955b57423bfe4de33df2b9fa255ce31d3ab9ba3acb8fdd8515bff:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b07d558ff1d54adebf502434a1a89aeb",
+      "statement": "On Windows, a .ps1 plugin is invoked via powershell -noprofile -nologo with the script path rather than executed directly.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://internal/plugin/plugin.go#L60-L71",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e9338d85e80f00b0a304c096831209aa2611c9c4c7e7989b52e16552ad2c3c33:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_56933b6217e34eac8bb920981d77ea3e",
+      "statement": "plugin.GetURL returns repository URLs for well-known plugins (currently only kms -> step-kms-plugin), used by app.Action to give download guidance when a plugin is missing.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://internal/cmd/root.go#L134-L147",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:56c45194db2cbfb799873941847c9c876dd1b71515f9e3a461ca7fab4bf00767:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://internal/plugin/plugin.go#L74-L82",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e343acce7ca6f58483aa97b627b886e14ebcaaaf46a5fd6387e6d7370b78739b:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-12T20:38:13.856Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/architecture/token-claims.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/architecture/token-claims.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/architecture/token-claims.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:b086e2422fcb24181436c500643e2ca77297c421c2ec2e88963f863425989f3d",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c9896e9096a44173be85652524f9aa2a",
+      "statement": "DefaultClaims seeds a JWT with issuer 'step-cli', audience 'https://ca/sign', and a default validity of 5 minutes beginning at the current UTC time.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://token/token.go#L117-L130",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c2734c9d11850ffab88536b9f8428d0ca6017e99abb8c181587d19e8b6d61e24:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_728304f7ed294a73a16b5591fa82de81",
+      "statement": "Claims.Sign builds a JWT signer, computes a kid header from the SHA256 thumbprint of the signing key, and compact-serializes the signed token; a single aud value is forced to a string.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://token/token.go#L70-L104",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e172a43f85107bddab7ba8baab6e4ff0505bf0bb98f19f498e6a948da4989ba2:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_04861beeb2804a3c85851550b2455c3d",
+      "statement": "token/options.go exposes With* functional options to set sha, sans, step, user, cnf, validity, issuer, subject, audience, jwt ID, kid, x5c, nebula, and sshpop claims/headers on a token.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://token/options.go#L27-L362",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f97ca94258af676b6af1d04059c46334eccfeb9e813f0443d4c3562633184be9:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_2e6fe3a28bbb46b3abe27ed81cf411fb",
+      "statement": "WithValidity enforces strict token validity bounds: minimum 10s, maximum 1h, and a maximum 30-minute allowed delay between now and the start of the validity window.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://token/options.go#L146-L168",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b144ebc7f953d5aba0cd25ae9547892afec7103e1d8bcd50918848c6fad9a0b:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://token/token.go#L11-L24",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3e8f611f0b655155c2b0161387c2838bad216d0b53e910180096bf75f2c1671a:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d33fa9063975458688c5f320e6fb8bcc",
+      "statement": "WithConfirmationFingerprint/WithFingerprint attach a cnf claim whose x5rt#S256 value is the base64url SHA256 fingerprint of a CSR or SSH public key, used for proof-of-possession.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://token/options.go#L110-L144",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:79e4c1087dca41343b8d7dc54919224cd828df9a6a58907ce99adced41605d6b:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a58789c2067c4a6fbab2da8b7034f5bd",
+      "statement": "Payload.Type() discriminates tokens as GCP, AWS, Azure, K8sSA (issuer kubernetes/serviceaccount), JWK (sha/sans present), OIDC, or Unknown.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://token/parse.go#L64-L82",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b6ded519c51e95ec8a89abd9b5278db5b992b3775542cb82177ce0861501abe1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_30a30744731346a3ab97fe0ba88bba8e",
+      "statement": "Parse verifies the token signature before decoding claims, while ParseInsecure decodes claims without verification.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://token/parse.go#L139-L166",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ebedd4e4a891c3791f37dd10d799eccb896ceb2fbf5938b25662ddfe16808bcf:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_5dff84d6c91c48d58681509c757fc2d4",
+      "statement": "On parse, AWS tokens unmarshal the amazon.document into an instance identity document and Azure tokens parse the xms_mirid claim into subscription/resource-group/type/name attributes.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://token/parse.go#L168-L189",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7f933744d8e7ebefe3322debca5c83e556cba124ca6c92a414e23f7ad9d6c9fb:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-12T20:38:13.856Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/architecture/token-flows.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/architecture/token-flows.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/architecture/token-flows.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:7a192d55c4ff1e751faafd49122404da061f63a7c7bd90bba9c6ab9b8b993dac",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a85a770f8dfd430788608e412f39e2d1",
+      "statement": "CertificateFlow wraps either an OfflineCA (offline mode) or nothing, and its NewCertificateFlow applies options to a package-global sharedContext, requiring --ca-config in offline mode.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/certificate_flow.go#L36-L131",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:23f4f7ce5c4e8d36766bf5ef4b2874db0cdc82df1cf24bd2ad9aa3850f48118d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_6dc2b69320fd4e23b6526519c8a47bf4",
+      "statement": "CertificateFlow.GetClient returns the offline client in offline mode; online it resolves --ca-url/--root, derives the CA URL and root SHA from bootstrap/provisioning tokens, or requires --ca-url and --root.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/certificate_flow.go#L134-L171",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eac06e54a30b1c44b73cef0ba05ec80a593dabe45011372e61bc7bd15ba6eeb7:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_41894e59f36944be9682589443abcf92",
+      "statement": "CertificateFlow.Sign submits an api.SignRequest and writes the returned certificate chain to a file.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/certificate_flow.go#L250-L293",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8654de214fa86c88ffdb297c7897329957a58767f3abf236bb47bc861c3ece08:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d2e09722da234263a698ba92bddb7084",
+      "statement": "CertificateFlow.CreateSignRequest derives default SANs per token type, including AWS instance identity, GCP compute-engine, Azure resource name, and OIDC email/subject/issuer-based SANs.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/certificate_flow.go#L297-L405",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fe53899bde3bce36ab21793922c426824f2a4864808cc9c7d2c810ac5d3b3c55:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9c0ff280407f46a68200fbc1be8e66fb",
+      "statement": "NewTokenFlow builds the audience URL from --ca-url (per token type), fetches provisioners via pki.GetProvisioners, prompts for a provisioner, and dispatches token generation by provisioner type.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/token_flow.go#L101-L183",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a206beb644478060eeb535b0495937c744cf645f516ffc3684fa13fa81394d6d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_dbd950d894d3430699b056d6a804e535",
+      "statement": "In NewTokenFlow, ACME and SCEP provisioners return dedicated error types because they do not support token auth flows.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/token_flow.go#L176-L179",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8b08f29870cf2a988ce7004d51815db2932d6ce96f99525bfd3e7d61a6aa6427:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/token_flow.go#L78-L99",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2b22ecbc1de1e48820a6c22911234603b546c5cfc8ce8b4728933278d9b2d97d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_6ca74d43bd91405f8a55f6d9d5430757",
+      "statement": "OfflineTokenFlow either uses an OfflineCA built from ca.json or command-line flags (--provisioner, --key, --kid) to generate a JWK or X5C token; the two paths are mutually exclusive with ca.json taking priority.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/token_flow.go#L212-L273",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e5545ce9d5f6f123130d7bb8540c83843366521759f35c9f488b0fd721c4ed4:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_28cba3c169c04c41a34f36b40d43a600",
+      "statement": "NewOfflineCA reads a ca.json config, requires at least one provisioner, and is a singleton to avoid double authority initialization.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L42-L81",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e92bb45ed2bb965fda7e92a8d8356a9c46ad5f747ce0ceabf20977f0c0839b54:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_6671b130645f4d8ea2eeda5704fa6c80",
+      "statement": "OfflineCA implements sign/renew/revoke/rekey/SSH operations as thin wrappers over an in-process certificates.Authority, authorizing each OTT before the operation.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L196-L440",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b3823cbff30b9de6003dea802fc7d9ba29a1026c6b5532933db3d2a8ca3816c1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_2798474ea2054e49a627e4614c8fbc25",
+      "statement": "NewClient selects offline (with required --ca-config) or online (ca-url/root) mode, defaulting the root to pki.GetRootCAPath(); admin clients additionally require admin cert/key for mTLS.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/client.go#L52-L122",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a61f9d701f5b076215cfeab64154c7a5899493cc7e1be1f51496409a9fb69010:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-12T20:38:13.856Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/certificates/certificate-commands.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/certificates/certificate-commands.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/certificates/certificate-commands.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:4df118a5ec2bdc49ba03b64dedb549ad98aa7306cfc0bc2c78ee5c28b7b65dd2",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_7d6d1cda66e44b0d9a61d1c919c48218",
+      "statement": "step certificate create supports profiles leaf, intermediate-ca, root-ca, and self-signed, plus generating a CSR with --csr, with self-signed requiring --subtle.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/certificate/create.go#L25-L39",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6048ecba123bae1cafb5467496791beb75fc05b0443ab1acb6a81a69d9f5e90c:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_af6ef49bceec489ca9c5ee6b2af450c5",
+      "statement": "Default certificate validities are per profile: 24h for leaves, 10 years for intermediates and roots, and 24h for template-based certificates.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/certificate/create.go#L33-L39",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8d082b4b86dda37faec4f0beebd792d0a88d8db7073d8708aa52600d3102a719:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_3ed6d7f7f6bc4d8b8e7a4d44c89e8278",
+      "statement": "create generates a new key with keyutil using --kty/--curve/--size defaults (EC P-256) when --key is absent, and rejects --kty/--curve/--size when --key is supplied.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/certificate/create.go#L773-L836",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d90f729ac95dcbfd0b03f14229f56faaed9304d411164b3dfa564e490d605d55:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_54135e86132149d6941f0c0c99119f54",
+      "statement": "create private keys are encrypted on write unless --no-password is combined with --insecure.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://command/certificate/create.go#L911-L933",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:35c2010109b3c7b264f98cfeb5b7581c4e96fbc0756580c0a460823bfebc6988:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_6a03a4aa84614804a566d68d49a5d1f7",
+      "statement": "create templates customize the certificate/CSR via a Go text/template-based JSON template (--template), with .Subject, .SANs, and user data from --set/--set-file; --template and --profile are mutually exclusive.",
+      "evidence": [
